      "writtenOn": "2022-12-20T20:45:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We may be able to make this particular comment more concise for clarity.\nMaybe:\n```\nAssuming there is an active tracing session, this call will create a trace event  if tracing is enabled (or if force_always_trace is true). The event goes through Atrace by default but can go to Perfetto by calling SkAndroidFrameworkTraceUtil::setUsePerfettoTrackEvents(true).\n\nIf force_always_trace \u003d true, then the caller *must* append the \".always\" suffix to the provided category. This allows Perfetto tracing sessions to optionally filter to just the \"skia.always\" category tag.\n```\n\nCould we add a check if skia is set to debug that logs or otherwise reports debug output if the category is not correctly formatted (ie, that \".always\" is appended to categories that should always be traced)? That way, it doesn\u0027t really impede tracing unless someone is actively trying to debug.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 262,
        "startChar": 3,
        "endLine": 271,
        "endChar": 16
      },
      "revId": "422fed58e7d2b93a6f6f3a4c18b2156e5590e57a",
